Optional template layers (not in this repository; you build them)
------------------------------------------------------------------
`recipes/ci-pylibs/` installs Python packages into a template layer from wheels that `fetch-wheels.sh` downloads from PyPI, so their licenses apply to
the template you build and to anyone you give it to. At the versions fetched on 2026-11-05 (the exact versions are whatever PyPI serves on the day you fetch):
BSD-3-Clause: numpy (its wheel also bundles OpenBLAS and the GCC runtime libraries, with their own terms: BSD, GPL-3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception,
Zlib, MIT, CC0), pandas, scipy (bundles OpenBLAS and libgfortran as above), scikit-learn, joblib, threadpoolctl, contourpy, cycler, httpcore, httpx, idna,
python-dateutil, lxml (bundles libxml2 and libxslt, MIT), cloudpickle, kiwisolver, mpmath, sympy, seaborn.
MIT: beautifulsoup4, soupsieve, anyio, h11, charset-normalizer, et_xmlfile, fonttools, narwhals, openpyxl, pyparsing, PyYAML, urllib3.
Apache-2.0: requests, tzdata; packaging (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause). MPL-2.0: certifi, tqdm (MPL-2.0 AND MIT). PSF: matplotlib (a PSF-style license), typing_extensions.
MIT-CMU (HPND): pillow, whose wheel bundles freetype, harfbuzz, libpng, libtiff, lcms2, openjpeg and others under their own licenses.
Nothing here is copyleft in a way that reaches your own code through use, but redistributing a template means redistributing these packages and the bundled
GPL-with-exception runtime libraries: keep the license files inside the wheels' `*.dist-info` directories in the image.

